# Git and GitHub Complete Guide for DevOps

## Overview
This shows Git and GitHub fundamentals used in real-world DevOps and software development workflows. It covers version control concepts, Git architecture, common commands, branching strategies, and collaboration using GitHub.

## Version Control System (VCS)
A Version Control System helps track changes made to files over time. It enables collaboration, maintains history, and allows rollback to previous versions.

## Types of Version Control Systems
1. Local VCS
2. Centralized VCS (CVCS)
3. Distributed VCS (DVCS)

Git is a Distributed Version Control System where each developer has a complete copy of the repository and its history.

## Advantages of Git
- Faster performance
- Offline access
- Better collaboration
- Easy branching and merging
- Full project history available locally

## Git Architecture
- Working Directory
- Staging Area
- Local Repository
- Remote Repository

## Installing Git
sudo apt update
sudo apt install git -y

Verify installation:
git --version

## Git Configuration
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your.email@example.com"

Check configuration:
git config --list

## Initializing a Repository
git init

## Checking Repository Status
git status

## Adding Files to Staging Area
git add filename
git add .

## Committing Changes
git commit -m "commit message"

## Viewing Commit History
git log

## Undoing Changes
git reset --soft HEAD~1
git reset --hard HEAD~1

## Branching
Create a branch:
git branch branch-name

Switch branch:
git checkout branch-name

Create and switch branch:
git checkout -b branch-name

## Merging Branches
git merge branch-name

## GitHub
GitHub is a cloud-based platform used to host Git repositories and collaborate with teams.

## Creating a GitHub Repository
1. Create a repository on GitHub
2. Copy the repository URL

Connect local repo to GitHub:
git remote add origin https://github.com/username/repository-name.git

Push code to GitHub:
git push -u origin main

## Pulling Changes from Remote
git pull origin main

## Cloning a Repository
git clone https://github.com/username/repository-name.git

## Fork
Fork creates a personal copy of another user's repository to work independently.

## Pull Request
Pull requests are used to submit changes for review before merging into the main branch.

## Git Ignore
Create .gitignore file to exclude files:
*.log
.env
node_modules/

## Common Git Commands
git init
git status
git add .
git commit -m "message"
git log
git branch
git checkout
git merge
git push
git pull
git clone

## Key Learnings
- Version control concepts
- Git command-line usage
- Branching and merging
- GitHub collaboration workflow
- DevOps-ready source code management

## Conclusion
Git and GitHub are essential tools for DevOps engineers. Understanding these concepts ensures efficient collaboration, reliable code tracking, and smooth CI/CD workflows.
